---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Supply — PATTERNFORMS"
  description="The manufacturing arm of PatternForms. We procure, machine, and supply the components and assemblies behind PatternForms and PatternHouse projects."
  canonical="https://pattern-forms-website.vercel.app/supply"
>
  <div class="pf-page">
    <section class="pf-container">

      <div class="pf-rail-grid">
        <div class="pf-rail">
          <p class="pf-eyebrow" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">04 · SUPPLY</p>
          <div><strong>FUNCTION</strong></div>
          <div>MANUFACTURING</div>
          <div style="margin-top: 8px;"><strong>MATERIALS</strong></div>
          <div>ENGINEERED TIMBER</div>
          <div style="margin-top: 8px;"><strong>METHOD</strong></div>
          <div>DfMA</div>
          <div style="margin-top: 8px;"><strong>OUTPUT</strong></div>
          <div>KIT-OF-PARTS<br />OR ASSEMBLED</div>
        </div>

        <div class="pf-supply-body">
          <p class="pf-body">
            The parts behind every PatternForms project — born from the same system as the design.
          </p>
          <p class="pf-body">
            Supply is the manufacturing arm of PatternForms. Here we procure, machine, and supply
            the components and assemblies behind PatternForms and PatternHouse projects.
          </p>
          <p class="pf-body">
            Our buildings are designed from the part up — to complement the multi-faceted
            requirements of our system through an exacting design process.
          </p>
          <p class="pf-body">
            What the Studio creates, Supply delivers, and nothing is lost in translation between them.
            This is done through our systemised work.
          </p>
          <p class="pf-body">
            We bring deep experience in engineered timber and the supply chains behind it, and we apply
            Design for Manufacture and Assembly (DfMA) principles — so every component is designed
            for the way it is made, moved, and put together.
          </p>
          <p class="pf-body" style="color: var(--pf-grey-60);">
            Our workshop utilises highly accurate CNC machines and robots to ensure industrial
            tolerances meet our system specification. This means we are able to provide building
            components as a kit-of-parts, or fully assembled, depending on project requirements.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .pf-supply-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 36px;
    max-width: 720px;
  }
</style>
